**Whole stack on/off:** `~/studio-stack.sh stop|start [service]` and `status [--tsv]` (source `studio-stack.sh`
in the repo, copied by hand; services: swap image music classify ocr asr omniasr openviking searxng ollama; `swap` is
llama-swap, which runs every LLM). The Claude Code mod `studio-services` (`/studio`) draws a pane in two sections:
**LLMs on demand** (llama-swap's models with state and RAM, Load/Unload and Unload all: `~/studio-stack.sh
load|unload [MODEL]`; `status --tsv` adds `llm<TAB>id<TAB>loaded|starting|unloaded<TAB>description` lines) and
**Services** (each with Start/Stop, ComfyUI included), plus "Use Ornith" / "Use vLLM": `~/studio-stack.sh default
ornith|vllm [MODEL]` sets Pi's default in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json`, and the mod rewrites dsh's
`agent-default-model` in the MacBook's `~/.dsh/splash.patch.yml` (`install.sh` resets it to `ornith`). Switching
starts no server: the first request loads the model. The engine model switch (`studio-stack.sh model`) is gone
(2026-11-14): both vLLM and both Splash models are separate llama-swap models. `stop` frees RAM for ComfyUI
(`127.0.0.1:8188`): it stops llama-swap (and every model it runs),
boots out the LaunchAgent services and OpenViking, runs `searxng.sh down`, stops Colima and kills Ollama
(the app respawns its server, so both). It refuses while image/music-server is generating (`FORCE=1`
overrides). `start` brings them back, then loads the llama-swap models named in `LLMS` (default none), except classify, asr and omniasr: off by default since 2026-11-11 (`OFF_BY_DEFAULT`), started only by name, and stopping one also `launchctl disable`s it so it stays off after a reboot (`start <name>` re-enables it). ComfyUI starts/stops only by name
(`start|stop comfyui` runs `~/ComfyUI/run_comfyui.sh` via nohup, log `~/comfyui.log`, or `stop_comfyui.sh`;
the pane has its button), never with stop/start all. It never touches studio-radar or sinhala-ocr. Stopped 2026-11-09 for ComfyUI: 76% memory free afterwards.

The SearXNG stack is a git checkout of `github.com/chan4lk/searxng-stack`. To
update it: `cd ~/searxng-stack && git pull && ./searxng.sh restart`. Its `.env`
holds the instance secret and is git-ignored, so never commit it.

### Splash

Splash runs under llama-swap (since 2026-11-14), one process per model, on loopback ports with no key of its own.
Both models are downloaded and can run at the same time (RAM allowing):

| Model (= llama-swap id) | Size on disk | llama-swap RAM | TTL |
|---|---|---|---|
| `incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-Splash` | 16 GB, dense | 18 GB | 30 min |
| `incoai/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Splash` | 20 GB, mixture of experts | 22 GB | 2 h (OpenViking's model) |

Clients send the model id to `http://__SERVER_IP__:8100` with Sushi's key: the MacBook's `claude-splash`,
`opencode-splash`, `pi-splash` and `dsh-splash`, and OpenViking's summaries and memory extraction. A model that is
idle loads on the next request (~10 s; the first request waits). Unloading one cuts off a reply in progress:
**ask before unloading a model someone is using.**

Splash is 1.1.0 (`brew upgrade splash`; the tap only refreshes after `brew update`).
`--max-cache-disk 40G` keeps evicted prompt caches on the SSD; context defaults
to 256K. Loading takes ~10 s.

Splash has no `/v1/embeddings` (404): it serves chat only (`/v1/chat/completions`,
`/v1/responses`, `/v1/messages`). Use Ollama for embeddings.

llama-swap's log (`~/Library/Logs/llama-swap.log`, or the web UI's logs) has Splash's one line per request, `input … cached … tools N · TTFT`,
which is the quickest way to see why a client is slow. A cold 85K-token prompt
takes about 2 minutes before the first output token.

### Sushi

[sushi](https://github.com/beamivalice/sushi) 1.2.1 (MIT, `brew install beamivalice/tap/sushi`; source checkout
read-only at `~/github_repos/sushi`) serves `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Sushi-3bpw` (80 GB in
`~/.sushi/models/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Sushi-3bpw`: 49.3 GiB weights + a 29.8 GiB n-gram table read from the SSD).
dsh's default model since 2026-10-09 (provider `sushi` in `~/.dsh/splash.settings.yaml`).

- **Runs under llama-swap** (since 2026-11-14) as `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Sushi-3bpw`, through
  `llama-swap/sushi.sh` (the old `~/sushi-serve.sh` settings: 4-bit KV, 256K context, vision; loopback, no key of its
  own). It claims 46 GB of llama-swap's 50 GB pool, so loading it unloads every other model.
- **Vision:** the script passes `--vision` (image tower +0.9 GB inside the SSD budget), so the dsh entry declares
  `input: [ text, image ]`. Verified 2026-10-10: it answers questions about images (OpenAI `image_url` parts).
- **Key:** `~/.sushi/api-key` on the Studio (passed by `--api-key-env`), copied to the MacBook's `~/.sushi-api-key`;
  the `dsh-splash` alias exports it as `SUSHI_API_KEY`. Without it: 401.
- **Memory:** the weights don't fit resident beside the other services, so routed experts stream from the SSD
  (MTP still runs). With `sudo sysctl iogpu.wired_limit_mb=59000` (resets at reboot; 59,000 is the 64 GB ceiling,
  above it macOS panics) the script keeps 44 GiB resident: 102–111 tok/s warm. Without it, 36 GiB: ~80 tok/s.
  `SUSHI_RESIDENT=1` loads fully resident with `--fast`, but that needs ~56 GiB free for 256K context; with Colima,
  Ollama and OpenViking running only ~53 GiB is free, which caps context at 34K (too small for dsh's ~12K-token
  prompt and tools). With those three and SearXNG stopped (2026-10-09) it loads at 256K: 104–111 tok/s warm, prefill
  of a short prompt ~170 ms vs ~370 ms streamed, 16% memory free.
- **It needs Splash, image-server, music-server and classify-server off.** They were stopped on 2026-10-09
  (`launchctl bootout` for the three LaunchAgents; `launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u)
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.searxng-stack.<name>.plist` brings one back). With Splash off, OpenViking's
  summaries and memory extraction fail until Splash runs again.

### Mellum

JetBrains' `Mellum2.1-12B-A2.5B-Thinking` (Apache-2.0; MoE, 64 experts top-8, 128K context, 3 of 4 layers
sliding-window) for coding and agentic tool use. Its `mellum` architecture is new: Sushi and Splash can't load it,
and mlx-lm 0.32.0 is the first release that can. It runs `mlx_lm.server` from `~/mellum/.venv` (uv, `mlx-lm==0.32.0`)
on the MXFP4 MLX quant `randmaru/Mellum2.1-12B-A2.5B-Thinking-mlx-mxfp4` (6.5 GB, in the HF cache).

- **Runs under llama-swap** (since 2026-11-14) as `Mellum2.1-12B-A2.5B` (alias: the repo id), JetBrains' sampling
  (temp 0.6, top_p 0.95, top_k 20), `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`. `~/mellum-serve.sh` (old port 8085) is no longer used.
- **API:** thinking comes back in `message.reasoning`, tool calls in `tool_calls` (both verified 2026-10-11).
- **dsh:** model `Mellum2.1-12B-A2.5B` of provider `studio`, text only. A dsh headless read-fix-run task took 17.6 s.
- **Memory:** ~3 GB RSS beside Sushi (19% free, ~1.7 GB swap used with both up).
- Official GGUFs (`JetBrains/Mellum2.1-12B-A2.5B-Thinking-GGUF`) need a llama.cpp that knows `mellum`; the
  Studio's Ollama 0.40.2 is untested with them.

### LFM

Liquid AI's `LFM2.5-24B-A2B` (LFM Open License v1.0, not Apache/MIT: check it before business use). A reasoning
MoE (`lfm2_moe`: 24B total, ~2B active, 64 experts top-4; 30 conv layers + 10 attention layers, so the KV cache
is small, ~2.6 GB at 128K). Official 8-bit MLX `LiquidAI/LFM2.5-24B-A2B-MLX-8bit` (25.5 GB, in the HF cache),
served by `mlx_lm.server` from Mellum's venv (`~/mellum/.venv`, mlx-lm 0.32.0; older releases load it but
route the experts wrong).

- **Runs under llama-swap** (since 2026-11-14) as `LFM2.5-24B-A2B` (alias: `LiquidAI/LFM2.5-24B-A2B-MLX-8bit`),
  Liquid's sampling (temp 0.1, top_k 50), `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`; ~23 s cold start. `~/lfm-serve.sh` (old port 8087)
  is no longer used.
- **Repetition penalty:** Liquid recommends 1.05, but `mlx_lm.server` has no flag for it; clients send
  `repetition_penalty` in the request body.
- **API:** thinking in `message.reasoning`, tool calls in `tool_calls` (verified 2026-10-16).
- **Measured 2026-10-16** (Ornith also up): ~91 tok/s warm (254 tokens in 2.8 s), tool call 1.5 s.
- **dsh:** model `LFM2.5-24B-A2B` of provider `studio`, text only.
- **Memory:** ~25 GB RSS; 73% free beside Ornith.
- **Strata** (`github.com/Niko1221/Strata`, MIT; checked 2026-10-15) serves only Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
  (and Unsloth's 4–6-bit files on Mac), so it can't run LFM or other models. Its Mac engine is Metal, built
  from source (not MLX). On 64 GB only Q2_0 fits (~46 GB resident + a 29 GB n-gram table on the SSD); Strata measured
  108–120 tok/s on an M5 Max, about the same as Sushi on the same model family. Not installed.

