- **Runs under llama-swap** (since 2026-11-14) as `Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B` (`HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`, model
  `local/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-GGUF:Q4_K_M`), 24 GB of the pool, 2 h TTL. Loads in ~20 s (the first start ever hashes
  the 20 GiB file once, ~30 s). `~/ornith-serve.sh` (old port 8086) is no longer used.
- **dsh:** provider `ornith` in `splash.patch.yml` (base URL :8100), `input: [ text, image ]`.
- **Pi on the Studio** (since 2026-11-09): `~/.pi/agent/models.json` has provider `ornith`
  (`baseUrl http://__SERVER_IP__:8100/v1`, `"apiKey": "!cat ~/.sushi/api-key"` so the key isn't copied in,
  text + image, 256K context, 32K output), and `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` makes it the default
  (`defaultProvider ornith`, `defaultModel Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B`). Ollama's `gemma4:e2b-mlx` is still there.
  Backups: `*.bak-20261109`, `*.bak-20261114*`. On the Studio itself use `http://__SERVER_IP__:8100` (llama-swap binds
  only the Tailscale IP; `__SERVER_NAME__` doesn't resolve). If llama-swap is down, Pi's default fails.
  Extensions in `~/.pi/agent/extensions/` (sources in `clients/pi/`, copied by hand, not by `install.sh`):
  `image-generate.ts` (see image-server) and `searxng-search.ts`, tool `searxng_search` (query, `max_results`
  default 8, `time_range`) against `http://127.0.0.1:8889` (`$SEARXNG_URL` overrides). The installed
  `@ollama/pi-web-search` package's `web_search`/`web_fetch` fail with `Unauthorized`: they go through
  Ollama to ollama.com, and the Studio's Ollama isn't signed in.
- **Measured 2026-10-11** (Mellum also up, Sushi off): ~175 tok/s (894 tokens in 5.1 s), tool call ~1 s,
  image question ~7 s, dsh headless read-fix-run task 11.9 s. 59% memory free with both up.
- **The GGUF is patched.** Splash 1.1.0 loads GDN `ssm_alpha`/`ssm_beta` only as Q8_0, F32 or BF16
  (`libexec/install/gguf.py`), and the official `ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-GGUF` stores them as Q4_K.
  `~/ornith/gguf_ssm_f32.py SRC DST` (run with `~/mellum/.venv/bin/python -I`, which has `gguf`) rewrites
  those 60 tensors as F32 (exact dequantization) and copies the other 693 byte for byte. The result is a
  local cache repo, `~/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--local--Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-GGUF/`, with `refs/main`
  naming a made-up 40-hex snapshot that also holds the mmproj (hard link). The untouched official download was
  deleted; to redo the patch, re-download `Ornith-1.5-35B-Q4_K_M.gguf` and the mmproj.
- **Splash takes only a repo id** (`OWNER/REPO[:VARIANT]`), never a local path. A local cache repo like the
  one above works with `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`.
- **What didn't work (2026-10-11):**
  - sushi 1.2.1 serves only `qwen4_exp`, `mimo_v2` and `glm5_next` (`ArchitectureUnsupported`), though its
    source mentions `qwen3_5_moe`.
  - The oMLX build `scottlowry/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-oQ4e-mtp` (deleted): Splash rejects its mixed 5/6/8-bit
    layers (`unsupported affine quantization for …linear_attn.in_proj_qkv`), and its config spells
    `rope_parameters.type` instead of `rope_type`.
  - Ornith's own `ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-DFlash` (deleted) is a DFlash v1 draft; Splash
    needs DFlash2.

### llama-swap (on-demand LLMs)

[llama-swap](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap) (MIT; v268, pinned with its SHA-256 in `llama-swap/llama-swap.sh`;
installed 2026-11-14) is one OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible endpoint, `http://__SERVER_IP__:8100/v1`, for every LLM in
`llama-swap/config.yaml`. A request's `model` starts that model's server on a loopback port; it unloads after 30 idle
minutes (`globalTTL`) or earlier when a newly requested model needs its RAM: the capacity router gives LLMs a 50,000 MB
`ram` pool and each model its `capacities.ram`, and evicts the fewest models to make room. API key: Sushi's
(`apiKeys`, from `STUDIO_API_KEY` set by the script); `Authorization: Bearer` and `x-api-key` both work.

- **Web UI:** `http://__SERVER_IP__:8100/ui` (browser login: any user name, Sushi's key as password): models,
  load/unload, live logs, activity.
- **Manage:** `cd ~/searxng-stack/llama-swap && ./llama-swap.sh install|status|logs|restart|validate`. `install`
  downloads the pinned release to `~/llama-swap/`, checks it, copies `config.yaml` there and (re)loads LaunchAgent
  `com.searxng-stack.llama-swap` (log `~/Library/Logs/llama-swap.log`). It runs with `-watch-config`: copying a changed
  `config.yaml` to `~/llama-swap/` reloads it (and unloads running models). `~/studio-stack.sh stop swap` stops it and
  every model it started.
- **Adding a model:** a `models:` entry with `cmd` (`${llama}` / `${mlx}` macros, `${PORT}`), `name`, `description`
  (the pane shows it), `capacities: { ram: MB }`; for mlx_lm.server also `useModelName` (repo id) and
  `checkEndpoint: /v1/models`. Then add it to the `studio` provider in dsh's template and Pi's `models.json`.
- **Models** (measured 2026-11-14; cold start = first request until the reply):

  | id | What | Files in `~/models/` or HF cache | RAM | Cold start |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `Qwen3.8-27B-FCF` | DavidAU's uncensored dense 27B merge (Apache-2.0), vision, MTP draft 2 (acceptance 79–92% in the log), ~37 tok/s, 128K | `qwen38-fcf/` MTP-Q5_K_M + mmproj-F16 | ~31 GB | 14 s |
  | `Qwen3.5-4B-3D-Coder` | ccore's early-preview Three.js / coding 4B (Apache-2.0), vision, no MTP (card), ~47 tok/s, 64K; reasons ~20K+ tokens before a scene | `qwen35-3d-coder/` Q8_0 + Qwen3.5-4B mmproj | ~7 GB | 3 s |
  | `LFM2.5-24B-A2B` | see LFM | HF cache | ~27 GB | 23 s |
  | `Mellum2.1-12B-A2.5B` | see Mellum | HF cache | ~4 GB | 6 s |

  3D Coder's card system prompt for Three.js: "Use only the Three.js core ES module from
  https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/0.160.0/three.module.min.js. Do not import addons or legacy
  examples/js paths; implement any camera controls directly inside the HTML." FCF's reasoning effort defaults to
  "xhigh" in its jinja template.
- **llama.cpp** is Homebrew 0.9.0 (upgraded from 0.5.0 on 2026-11-14 for `--spec-type draft-mtp`; shared with
  ocr-server and sinhala-ocr).
- **Clients:** dsh provider `studio` (`splash.patch.yml`) and Pi on the Studio provider `studio` (`~/.pi/agent/models.json`,
  backups `models.json.bak-20261114*`): `pi --provider studio --model Qwen3.5-4B-3D-Coder`. Defaults unchanged.
- **Also here** (since 2026-11-14, see their sections): both Splash models, Ornith, both vLLM models and Sushi.

### vLLM (vllm-metal, multi-user test)

vllm-metal 0.33.0 (Homebrew tap `vllm-project/vllm-metal`, `brew install vllm-project/vllm-metal/vllm-metal`;
private Python env, `vllm` on PATH; installed 2026-11-09). It serves **MLX models only** here: the patched Ornith GGUF
(`qwen35moe`) and Splash's own `.bin` layer format can't load. Model: `mlx-community/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-4bit` (19 GB,
in the HF cache; Ornith's base model, no clean MLX build of Ornith exists).

- **Runs under llama-swap** (since 2026-11-14): `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` and `Qwen3.5-9B-heretic` are separate models there
  (`vllm serve <repo> ${vllm_args}`; the model must come first: `--gpu-memory-utilization 0.5`, 128K context, prefix caching, reasoning parser `qwen3`, tool
  parser `qwen3_coder`). Each reserves its budget up front (28 GB footprint at 0.5, KV cache 277K–292K tokens;
  llama-swap counts 33 GB), so only one runs at a time. The old `vllm/vllm-serve.sh` (port 8088) is gone from the repo; `~/vllm-serve.sh` on the Studio is unused.
- **Second model**, downloaded 2026-11-10:
  `xtools-at/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-Qwen3.5-9B-UNCENSORED-heretic` (Apache-2.0, BF16 safetensors, 18 GB; vllm-metal loads plain HF
  safetensors too, not only MLX), served as `Qwen3.5-9B-heretic`. Reasoning, tool calls verified; ~25 tok/s single user.
